pastPayments.body:
Coupons and redemptions recorded in the period, and how each was split across packages.

**Net income** subtracts what you paid for that money:
- for a **redemption**, the purchase cost of the redeemed bonds without accrued coupon, plus the purchase fee;
- for the **first coupon** after a purchase, the accrued coupon you paid the seller, which this coupon returns;
- other coupons are income in full.
Payment fees are subtracted as well. In USD, the payment converts at its own rate and the cost at the purchase rate, so currency moves show up here.
